<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n39950" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπικύπτω</span></b> , pf.
			(v.infr.):—<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>bend
				oneself over, stoop over, bow down</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Art.</u>
				52
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Th.</u>
				239
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀρθὸς ἕστηκεν, μικρὸν ἐπικύπτων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>HA</u>
					522b18
				</span></i>
			; of the horn of the moon, <i><span class="en">
				Thphr.
				<u>Sign.</u>
				27
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. ἐπί τι</span>
			<i>stoop</i>
			<i>down</i> to get something, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Cyr.</u>
				2.3.18
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. ἐς βιβλίον</span>
			<i>pore over</i> a book, <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Herm.</u>
				2
			</span></i>; <i>lean upon</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>DMort.</u>
					6.2
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. τῷ συνεδρίῳ</span>
			<i>bend</i>
			<i>over towards</i> it, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>JTr.</u>
				11
			</span></i>: pf.
			part.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπικεκῡφώς</span>
			<i>habitually stooping</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Anaxandr.
				37
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
